## Owner-controlled contributions

Contributions are by invitation. Only collaborators approved by `vasiloglou`
receive write access. Public availability permits reading and forking; it does
not grant permission to modify this repository.

For all changes, including owner and coding-agent changes, use a topic branch and
submit a pull request. Never push directly to main, force-push it, or delete it. Resolve
review conversations before merging. `.github/CODEOWNERS` names `vasiloglou` for
all files.

While `vasiloglou` is the only collaborator, branch protection requires PRs with
zero required approving reviews. GitHub prohibits authors from approving their
own PRs, so the owner's explicit merge decision is the acceptance step. Coding
agents may merge only with the owner's explicit authorization. Protection applies
to administrators too, with no PR bypass. Cloud CI is not currently a required
status check; run the focused checks applicable to a change and record results.

Before granting another account write access, enable one required approving
review and required code-owner review. Its PRs will then require `vasiloglou`'s
recorded approval. PRs authored by `vasiloglou` will need another authorized code
owner, or work must be authored through a separately controlled contributor/bot
identity so `vasiloglou` can approve. Never create a shared reviewer identity or
approve a PR through a token belonging to its author.

For a public repository, use the collaborators-only interaction limit to prevent
outside PRs, issues and comments. GitHub limits this setting to six months; renew
it before its reported expiration. It cannot be enabled while the repository is
private. Check the live settings before claiming restrictions are enforced.

## Refactoring dependencies and compatibility

The measured layer map is [tools/gnd_layers.json](tools/gnd_layers.json).
Errors and schemas have infrastructure homes; documents, values and universe
serve model data and lookup; extensions compute facts below checker and
applicability. Registry descriptors live in branches. Runtime graph checks count
lazy and literal dynamic imports as well as top-level imports. Add every new
module to the map, preserve the clean-layer ratchet, and do not grow allowances.

Old module names retain explicit aliases in the
[shim inventory](.gnd-planning/milestones/code-refactoring/notes/shim-inventory.md).
Patch the defining module for moved algorithms and the actual public lookup seam
for consumer wrappers. Move tests pin alias identity and source-scan coverage;
retirement follows the approved plan's RF-D5 gate. Current source changes make
old release evidence unavailable until its separately selected controls run.

Peripheral dependency homes are public filesystem seams in safefs, the bounded
runner in process, trusted adapters in agents, and the independent synth oracle
package. Assurance follows _wire, core, inheritance, claims, evidence dependency
order; transport carries receipts. Payload assembly lives in payloads, and
export/witness services own their thin API wrappers. Old imports remain aliases.

### Model query and constraint family homes

Use gnd.model_index.ModelIndex.for_model(model) for detached model queries. Each
request keys a bounded snapshot cache by current full model content, with unsafe
canonical shapes bypassing the cache. Keep the existing strict/truthy primitive
policy explicit. Raw serialization and deliberately retained domain traversal
sites are individually listed in the RF6 query policy; additions need a reason
and a current behavior control.

Constraint adaptation, evaluation, witness projection, presentation, scope and
shape selection use gnd.constraint_families.FAMILIES. Keep shared refusal and
vacuity precedence outside family-specific algorithms. The production branch
evidence registry remains a separate inventory. Preserve every historical import
shim until a separately approved retirement after the first release following RF6.

def _enforce_d12(before: dict[str, Any], candidate: dict[str, Any]) -> None:
    before_hosted = [
        (host, canonical_json_text(item), item) for host, item in _constraints(before, hosted=True)
    ]
    before_counts = Counter(rendered for _, rendered, _ in before_hosted)
    candidates = [
        (host, canonical_json_text(item), item) for host, item in _constraints(candidate, hosted=True)
    ]
    # IK2: the proposed induced constraints a reviewed status change may claim
    # are those left over once every unchanged candidate copy has consumed its
    # exact match, so two candidates can never confirm one predecessor and an
    # unchanged copy can never be confirmed a second time. A claim is keyed by
    # the predecessor's host, so confirmation cannot also move the rule to
    # another fact type or the top level (review R3). Computed up front so the
    # single in-order pass below keeps every pre-IK2 refusal order.
    leftover = before_counts - Counter(rendered for _, rendered, _ in candidates)
    claimable: Counter[tuple[str | None, str]] = Counter()
    for host, rendered, item in before_hosted:
        if (
            leftover[rendered]
            and item.get("source") == "induced"
            and item.get("status") == "proposed"
        ):
            leftover[rendered] -= 1
            claimable[(host, canonical_json_text(_without_review(item)))] += 1

    for host, rendered, constraint in candidates:
        if _contains_audit_key(constraint.get("provenance", {})):
            raise EvolutionError(
                "operation audit actor/origin/time fields cannot enter constraint provenance"
            )
        if before_counts[rendered]:
            before_counts[rendered] -= 1
            continue

        source = constraint.get("source")
        status = constraint.get("status")
        modality = constraint.get("modality")
        provenance = constraint.get("provenance")
        if not isinstance(provenance, dict):
            provenance = {}
        if source != "induced" and "induction" in provenance:
            raise EvolutionError("provenance.induction is allowed only under source induced (D-12)")
        if source == "induced":
            if (status, modality) == ("proposed", "deontic"):
                if "reviewed_in" in provenance:
                    raise EvolutionError(
                        "new induced constraints cannot carry provenance.reviewed_in (D-12)"
                    )
                continue
            if status == "confirmed":
                reviewed_in = provenance.get("reviewed_in")
                predecessor = (host, canonical_json_text(_without_review(constraint)))
                if isinstance(reviewed_in, str) and reviewed_in.strip() and claimable[predecessor]:
                    claimable[predecessor] -= 1
                    continue
                raise EvolutionError(
                    "induced constraints become confirmed only as a reviewed status change "
                    "of an existing proposed induced constraint (D-12)"
                )
            raise EvolutionError("new induced constraints must be proposed/deontic (D-12)")
        if source == "llm-inferred":
            if (status, modality) != ("proposed", "deontic"):
                raise EvolutionError(
                    "new llm-inferred constraints must remain proposed/deontic (D-12)"
                )
        elif source in ("sample", "common-sense"):
            # VG2 (issue 218): row evidence and library evidence, as the growth
            # document has the host write them; never confirmed, never alethic.
            if (status, modality) != ("proposed", "deontic"):
                raise EvolutionError(
                    "new sample and common-sense constraints must be proposed/deontic (D-12)"
                )
        elif source == "user-supplied":
            if status != "confirmed":
                raise EvolutionError(
                    "owner-approved user-supplied constraints must be confirmed (D-12)"
                )
        else:
            raise EvolutionError(
                "new or changed constraints must be llm-inferred/proposed/deontic "
                "or user-supplied/confirmed (D-12)"
            )


def _json_ready(value: Any) -> Any:
    if hasattr(value, "model_dump"):
        return value.model_dump(mode="json")
    if isinstance(value, dict):
        return {str(key): _json_ready(item) for key, item in value.items()}
    if isinstance(value, (list, tuple)):
        return [_json_ready(item) for item in value]
    return value


def _surface_index(
    document: dict[str, Any],
    *,
    verbalization: str,
) -> dict[str, tuple[str, str]]:
    """Index every deterministic model surface by stable machine reference."""

    result: dict[str, tuple[str, str]] = {}

    def add(reference: str, surface: str, value: Any) -> None:
        if reference in result:
            raise EvolutionError(f"duplicate stable blast-radius reference {reference}")
        result[reference] = (surface, canonical_sha256(value))
            label="model",
        )
        before_sha256 = sha256_hex(before_bytes)
        if before_sha256 != proposal.expected_model_sha256:
            raise EvolutionError(
                "stale expected model identity before preview: "
                f"expected {proposal.expected_model_sha256}, observed {before_sha256}"
            )
        try:
            before_text = before_bytes.decode("utf-8")
        except UnicodeDecodeError as error:
            raise EvolutionError(f"model is not UTF-8: {error}") from error

        # The CURRENT model is validated first, and nothing reads its parsed
        # form before this line. `load_model` is what runs the alias/event guard
        # (T-01-02) and the two validation layers, so parsing the live bytes
        # ahead of it would both construct alias-bearing input the guard exists
        # to refuse and hand the gate below a document whose shapes nothing has
        # checked -- where `parameters: 1` raises TypeError instead of returning
        # a refusal.
        from ._includes import enforce_ownership, provided_history

        history = _include_input(provided_history, proposal, previous_includes)
        before_loaded_model, before_document = _load_model_document(
            before_bytes,
            label="current model",
            model_path=self._model_path,
            historical=history,
        )

        # Before the CANDIDATE is validated, deliberately. The gate reads only
        # the current model and the proposal's declared locators, so its answer
        # never depends on the candidate -- and running it later would make its
        # commonest case unreachable. Renaming a fact type an operation
        # references cannot produce a VALID candidate without also editing that
        # operation, which is itself gated; checking the candidate's form first
        # would therefore answer "your candidate is invalid, go fix the
        # operations", sending the author straight into the other half of the
        # same gate.
        if before_loaded_model.includes:
            if proposal.linked_projects:
                raise EvolutionIncludeError('include:unsupported-route: linked project evolution')
            _include_input(enforce_ownership, before_loaded_model, before_document, proposal.operations)
        _enforce_operations_gate(before_document, proposal)

        placed: list[tuple[int, str | None, list[Any], Any]] = []
        if before_loaded_model.includes:
            candidate_model, candidate_document, validation, declared_document = self._include_candidate(
                proposal, before_loaded_model, before_document, placed)
        else:
            candidate_model, candidate_document, validation = self._validated_candidate(
                proposal.candidate_model,
                declared_references=before_loaded_model.reference_populations,
            )
            declared_document = _apply_declared_operations(before_document, proposal.operations, placed=placed)
            if declared_document != candidate_document:
                raise EvolutionError("declared operations do not equal the canonical candidate model")
        _enforce_d12(before_document, candidate_document)
        # After the gate (18), candidate validation, replay equality and D-12
        # (all 3), so a preview written with issues is otherwise valid (spec D6).
        # The population option is judged here, after every proposal refusal
        # and before the policy walk that consumes its outcomes (UG2 spec §6.4,
        # review R8): its policy requirement, then the read.
        if check_population is not None and policy is None:
            raise EvolutionError("invalid request: --check-population requires --policy additive")
        policy_values = self._policy_values(
            before_loaded_model,
            proposal,
            policy,
            populated,
            population=self._population_runner(
                check_population,
                before_loaded_model,
                proposal,
                candidate_model,
                placed,
                declared_document,
                expected_population_sha256,
            ),
        )
        # After the policy and every refusal, and read by nothing below: the
        # report is advice (MG-R4), so it can neither pre-empt nor change one.
        shape_values = (
            {"shape_matches": shape_matches(before_loaded_model, candidate_model, proposal)}
            if shape_report
            else {}
        )

        verbalization_text = render_model_verbalization(candidate_model)
        before_verbalization_text = render_model_verbalization(before_loaded_model)
        before_blob = CommittedText.from_text(before_text, media_type="application/yaml")
        verbalization = CommittedText.from_text(
            verbalization_text,
            media_type="text/plain",
        )
        affected = tuple(sorted({operation.reference() for operation in proposal.operations}))
        blast_radius = _radius_for_models(
            proposal, before_loaded_model, candidate_model, before_document, candidate_document,
            before_verbalization_text, verbalization_text)
        breaking = breaking_operations(proposal.operations)
        if accepted_blast_radius_sha256 is not None and (
            not breaking or accepted_blast_radius_sha256 != blast_radius.report_sha256
        ):
            raise EvolutionError(
                "accepted blast radius does not match this proposal, current model, "
                "candidate model, and ordered report"
            )
        values: dict[str, Any] = {
            "proposal": proposal,
            "proposal_sha256": proposal.proposal_sha256,
            "before_model": before_blob,
            "candidate_model": proposal.candidate_model,
            "verbalization": verbalization,
            "validation": validation,
            "affected_references": affected,
            "breaking": breaking,
            "blast_radius": blast_radius,
            "accepted_blast_radius_sha256": accepted_blast_radius_sha256,
            # Present only under a policy: absent fields stay out of the
            # digest body, so a policy-free preview keeps its digest (MG-R1).
            **policy_values,
            **shape_values,
            **(_include_snapshot_values(before_loaded_model, candidate_model)
               if before_loaded_model.includes else {}),
        }
        digest_body = {key: _json_ready(value) for key, value in values.items()}
        digest_body["schema_version"] = proposal.schema_version
        preview = EvolutionPreview(
            schema_version=proposal.schema_version,
            **values,
            preview_sha256=canonical_sha256(digest_body),
        )
        if before_loaded_model.includes:
            _include_claim_cap(canonical_json_bytes(preview))
        return preview

    def _include_candidate(self, proposal, before, document, placed):
        from gnd.model import _composed_view

        from ._includes import included_delta

        if proposal.candidate_model.media_type not in {'application/yaml', 'application/x-yaml'}:
            raise EvolutionIncludeError('candidate model media type must be application/yaml')
        candidate = _include_input(_parse_model_text, proposal.candidate_model.text)
        if candidate.get('reference_populations', []) != before.reference_populations:
            raise EvolutionIncludeError('declared operations change reference populations')
        declared = _apply_declared_operations(document, proposal.operations, placed=placed)
        if declared != candidate:
            raise EvolutionIncludeError('declared operations do not equal the canonical candidate model')
        view = _include_input(_composed_view, proposal.candidate_model.text.encode('utf-8'),
                              source=self._model_path, root=self._model_path.parent, analysis=True)
        _include_input(_json_document, view.document, label='candidate model')
        changed = _include_input(included_delta, before, view)
        _enforce_operations_gate(document, proposal, include_changes=changed)
        if view.model is None:
            radius = _include_radius(proposal, before, view, document, candidate, changed=changed)
            _include_claim_cap(canonical_json_bytes(radius))
            raise EvolutionIncludeAnalysis(radius, view.issues, (*before._included, *view.included))
        return view.model, candidate, _validation_for(view.model, proposal.candidate_model), declared

    def _verified_include_preview(self, preview, before_bytes):
        from ._includes import enforce_ownership, historical_bytes

        if preview.before_includes is None or preview.candidate_includes is None:
            raise EvolutionIncludeError('invalid missing include snapshots')
        _include_claim_cap(canonical_json_bytes(preview))
        if preview.proposal.linked_projects:
            raise EvolutionIncludeError('include:unsupported-route: linked project evolution')
        history = _include_input(historical_bytes, preview.proposal, preview.before_includes)
        before, document = _load_model_document(before_bytes, label='current model at publication',
                                                model_path=self._model_path, historical=history)

